 "goal": {
  "id": "50/G",
  "goal": "Explain how a realistic walking-behavior model for system-controlled VR navigation is derived from empirical walking studies, modeled to produce slow-in-slow-out visual speed, and validated for realism and user preference while recognizing its limits for cybersickness.",
  "achieves": "It gives the learner a foundation for optimizing VR navigation as part of building XR systems and prepares the learner to address cybersickness minimization in the course."
 },
